# Contributing

This document defines the delivery workflow for human and AI contributors. It
does not define a feature's product architecture.

## Baseline And Branch

1. Start from the latest approved base branch, normally `main`.
2. Inspect the working tree; do not include unrelated files.
3. Follow `docs/README.md` and inspect code/tests before changing anything.
4. Create a dedicated branch. Never implement a feature directly on `main`.

## Architecture And Implementation

- For complex changes, obtain architecture approval before implementation.
- Keep changes within approved scope and use reviewable commits.
- Add tests with the behavior they protect.
- Run the project-specific focused and full verification gates before opening a
  Pull Request.

## Documentation Impact Gate

Every Pull Request must evaluate these categories. Update each affected
document in the same Pull Request or provide a code-backed reason it is
unaffected.

| Change | Canonical location | Update point |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Changed implemented behavior | Relevant Knowledge Base map | Same PR as code |
| Changed test ownership/boundary | Test coverage map | Same PR as tests |
| Architecture decision | Reviewed design document | Before implementation; status after delivery |
| New project-specific engineering procedure | Relevant Skill | After reuse is demonstrated; adapter starter Skills may be adopted when applicable and their playbook origin is recorded |
| Deferred risk | Production-readiness backlog | PR deciding the deferral |
| Executed manual evidence | Acceptance document | After actual execution |
| Current project status | Live README/roadmap | Milestone closeout |
| Released behavior | Release notes | Before release tag |

Do not update documents mechanically. Knowledge Base maps contain technical
facts; Skills contain reusable methods; designs contain decisions; acceptance
records contain executed evidence. Keep explicitly dated release snapshots
historical.

## Pull Requests

Each Pull Request description includes:

- objective and scope;
- requirement-to-change and requirement-to-test traceability;
- exact local verification results;
- known limitations and deferred work;
- a completed Documentation Impact section;
- dependency information for a stacked PR.

Stop for independent review. Do not self-merge unless project ownership has
explicitly changed this policy.

## Merge And Release Gates

A Pull Request may merge only when review approves it, required CI is green on
its exact head, no Blocker/Major remains, and required documentation is current.

After merge, confirm CI on the resulting `main` commit. For a milestone or
release, execute required manual acceptance, record only observed results,
perform documentation closeout, and then create a tag from the green accepted
commit.
